es the zone with other high-attraction booths; moving it east separates their visitor crowds.\n\n- B10 target (16.5, 13.5) → (22.5, 13.5)\n\n## Iteration history\n\n| Iteration | Max density (p/m²) | p90 travel (s) | Completed | Errors | Comparable |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 | 3.69 | 279.2 | 82.5% | 0 | yes |\n| 1 | 3.14 | 281.9 | 86.5% | 0 | yes |\n| 2 | 3 | 282.6 | 85.5% | 0 | yes |\n\n## Assumptions\n\n- Pedestrian metrics come from the engine's JuPedSim simulation; one scenario and seed per run, so results are a single sample, not a distribution.\n- Booth popularity values are planning estimates of relative attraction, taken as given.\n- Densities are peak values per grid cell over the run; hotspot thresholds are the engine's. Travel times count finished agents only.\n- Geometric checks cover booth/obstacle/door-clearance/aisle rules only; egress capacity, fire code and accessibility were not assessed.\n- Analysis and revision proposals by `stub`; all metrics and coordinates in this report are computed by tools.\n\n## Unconfirmed items\n\n- Ceiling height not shown on plan (from floor plan)\n- Emergency door D-emg swing direction unconfirmed (from floor plan)\n\n---\n\n_This is a planning draft produced by an AI agent from simulation output. It is not a permit, fire-code or crowd-safety certification; a qualified reviewer must confirm it against the venue's actual conditions and applicable regulations._\n"},{"type":"step","data":{"id":"step-3-report-0","iteration":3,"step":"report","status":"done","title":"Write review report"}},{"type":"report","data":{"markdown":"# Layout revision report — Sample Hall A (40m x 30m)\n\n> This is a planning draft produced by an AI agent from simulation output. It is not a permit, fire-code or crowd-safety certification; a qualified reviewer must confirm it against the venue's actual conditions and applicable regulations.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe agent started from an entrance-first draft layout of Sample Hall A (40m x 30m) and simulated it under one fixed scenario. The worst congestion is hotspot #0. High-attraction booth B10 draws visitors into this zone.\n\nAcross 2 revisions it kept the layout as stable as possible and changed only what the simulation pointed at: High-attraction booth B10 sits in the entrance inflow; requiring popular booths to keep a distance from entrances separates arriving visitors from booth crowds; then Hotspot #0 persists next to B10, which shares the zone with other high-attraction booths; moving it east separates their visitor crowds. Each revised layout was re-validated and re-simulated with the identical scenario, so the before/after comparison below reflects layout changes only.\n\nThe run stopped because: max density 3 ≤ target 3 p/m² with no validation errors. Treat the result as a planning draft for human review; the items under Unconfirmed must be checked on site before the plan is relied on.\n\n## Before / after\n\nIdentical conditions for every iteration: scenario `browse`, 200 agents, 300 s, seed 42, density grid 2 m (fingerprint `93053505`). Target: max density ≤ 3 p/m² with no validation errors.\n\n| Metric | Baseline (iteration 0) | Final (iteration 2) | Change |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Max density | 3.69 p/m² | 3 p/m² | −0.69 p/m² (−18.7%) |\n| p90 travel time | 279.2 s | 282.6 s | +3.4 s (+1.2%) |\n| Mean travel time | 206.4 s | 204.7 s | −1.7 s (−0.8%) |\n| Completed fraction | 82.5% | 85.5% | +3 pt |\n| Hotspots | 4 | 5 | +1 |\n| Validation errors | 0 | 0 | ±0 |\n\nStop reason: **target met** — max density 3 ≤ target 3 p/m² with no validation errors.\n\n## What changed and why\n\n**Revision after iteration 0 → 1.** High-attraction booth B10 sits in the entrance inflow; requiring popular booths to keep a distance from entrances separates arriving visitors from booth crowds.\n\n- popular_door_distance 0 → 12 m\n\n**Revision after iteration 1 → 2.** Hotspot #0 persists next to B10, which shares the zone with other high-attraction booths; moving it east separates their visitor crowds.\n\n- B10 target (16.5, 13.5) → (22.5, 13.5)\n\n## Iteration history\n\n| Iteration | Max density (p/m²) | p90 travel (s) | Completed | Errors | Comparable |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 | 3.69 | 279.2 | 82.5% | 0 | yes |\n| 1 | 3.14 | 281.9 | 86.5% | 0 | yes |\n| 2 | 3 | 282.6 | 85.5% | 0 | yes |\n\n## Assumptions\n\n- Pedestrian metrics come from the engine's JuPedSim simulation; one scenario and seed per run, so results are a single sample, not a distribution.\n- Booth popularity values are planning estimates of relative attraction, taken as given.\n- Densities are peak values per grid cell over the run; hotspot thresholds are the engine's. Travel times count finished agents only.\n- Geometric checks cover booth/obstacle/door-clearance/aisle rules only; egress capacity, fire code and accessibility were not assessed.\n- Analysis and revision proposals by `stub`; all metrics and coordinates in this report are computed by tools.\n\n## Unconfirmed items\n\n- Ceiling height not shown on plan (from floor plan)\n- Emergency door D-emg swing direction unconfirmed (from floor plan)\n\n---\n\n_This is a planning draft produced by an AI agent from simulation output. It is not a permit, fire-code or crowd-safety certification; a qualified reviewer must confirm it against the venue's actual conditions and applicable regulations._\n","baselineIteration":0,"finalIteration":2}},{"type":"done","data":{"status":"completed","stopReason":"target_met","iterations":3,"baselineIteration":0,"finalIteration":2,"baseline":{"max_density":3.6923,"p90_travel_time_s":279.24,"mean_travel_time_s":206.35,"completed_fraction":0.825,"violations":0,"warnings":0,"hotspots":4,"truncated":false},"final":{"max_density":3,"p90_travel_time_s":282.6,"mean_travel_time_s":204.684,"completed_fraction":0.855,"violations":0,"warnings":0,"hotspots":5,"truncated":false}}}]}
